PopGBA - License
================

PopGBA is an unofficial port of the gpSP Game Boy Advance emulator
(libretro edition) to the SHARP Brain PW-G5300 (Windows CE, ARM). Its
license has two levels.

1. PopGBA as a whole: the GNU GPL, version 2 (same terms as upstream)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

PopGBA as a whole (AppMain.exe, and the source published in this
repository) is distributed under the GNU General Public License,
version 2 (GPL-2.0), on the same terms as upstream gpSP. The full text
of the GPL version 2 is in COPYING at the repository root.

This file does not state whether a later version of the GPL may also
be chosen: the upstream files are not consistent about it. Many gpSP
sources (main.c, section 3 below, among them) say "version 2 of the
License, or (at your option) any later version", but some files built
into AppMain.exe carry no license notice of their own (for example
memmap.c, gba_cc_lut.c, bios_data.S, gpsp_config.h, gba_over.h,
libretro/libretro.c and libretro/libretro_core_options.h), and
upstream's README states no license. See CE/LICENSING.md, section 1.

The GPL allows redistribution, including commercial use, on its terms:
keep the license and the copyright notices, make the corresponding
source available with any binary, and keep derived works as a whole
under the GPL. There is no warranty.

2. PopGBA's own code: MIT
----------------------------------------------------------------------

This MIT license covers only PopGBA's own code listed in
CE/LICENSING.md (the files marked "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT": the
CE/ frontend except the font data, the mascot image and the icon).
PopGBA as a whole is distributed under the GPL (section 1).

